      "textEn": "He who is attached to them, even after death, does not see. For self-satisfaction, such people believe that their nation, community, or family will save them. They remain unaware that soldiers who make such a mistake will be destroyed chronologically.\nWill be destroyed. In conclusion, man should associate with those who are engaged in devotion 24 hours a day. The tongue does not utter the names of the Lord's virtues.\nThe mind does not remember His lotus feet. Krishna, I bow to you, even once.\nTanaanayadhvamasato'krutavishnukrityaan. 29. Meaning of the word\n\nJihvā—tongue; na—not; vakti—singing; bhagavat—complete supreme; guna—divine qualities; naam—name;\nand of the holy name; dheyam—giving; chetah—heart; cha—also; na—not; smarati—recites; tat—his;\ncharan-arvindam—the lotus feet; krishnaya—to Lord Krishna, through his archa-vigraha in the temple; no—not;\nnamati—bowing; yat—whose; shirah—head; ekada api—even once; tan—them; aanayadhvam—bringing before me\nAao; Asatah—to the devotees; Aakrita—not done; Vishnu-kritya—duty towards Lord Vishnu. Oh my dear devotees! You people should only bring to me those sinful men whose tongues\ndo not chant the name and virtues of Krishna, whose hearts do not even once remember the lotus feet of Krishna,\nand whose heads do not bow before Krishna even once. Send to those people who do not fulfill their duties towards Vishnu, which\nare the only duties of human life. Bring all those stupid and wicked people to me! Meaning: In this verse, the word 'Vishnu-krityan' is very important because the purpose of human life\nis to please Lord Vishnu. The Varna system is also for this purpose. As it is said in\nVishnu Purana (3.8.9)—\n\nVarnashramacharavat purushena parah puman. Vishnu is worshipped, there is no other path for him."
