      "textEn": "Human society is such that it strictly follows that Varnaashrama Dharma which society\ndivides into four social divisions (Brahmin, Kshatriya, Vaishya and Shudra) and four spiritual divisions\n(Brahmacharya, Grihastha, Vanaprastha and Sanyas). Varnaashram Dharma brings man closer to God,\nVishnu, which is the only true goal of human society. They do not know.\nVishnu is the path of selfishness—but unfortunately, people do not know that their selfishness is in returning to the abode of God,\nor in reaching Lord Vishnu. Durashayi ya bahirarthamaninah—contrasting with this, they\nremain only deluded. It is expected from every human that one should perform their duty to reach Lord Vishnu. Therefore, Yamraj advises the messengers of Yama to bring those people to him\nwho have forgotten their duty towards Lord Vishnu (Akrutavishnukrityaan).\nHe who does not chant the holy name of Vishnu,\nwho does not bow his head to the image of Vishnu,\nand who does not remember the lotus feet of Lord Vishnu, is punishable by Yama. In short, all non-Vaishnava rites are liable for punishment by Yama. That which is capable of that, that Lord, the ancient one,\nNarayana, by his own power, what is unmade. Salutations to the one who is the ocean of nectar, the creator of the knowledgeable, the one with lotus-like eyes.\nSalutations to the man who is the ocean of peace, the one who is on the earth. 30>. Meaning of the word\n\nTat—That; Kshamyatam—Forgive; Sah—That; Bhagavan—The supreme being; Purushah—The supreme being;\nPuranah—The most ancient; Narayanah—Narayan; Swa-Purusha-him—By your servants; Yat—That which; Asat—Undeserving; Krutam—\nProsperous; Nah—Our; Swanaam—Of our own people; Aho—Alas; Nabhividusham—Without knowing; Rachit-Aanjalinam—To you\nWith folded hands, asking for forgiveness; Kshanti—Forgiveness; Gariyasi—Is glorious; Namah—Salutations; Purushaya—To the supreme being; Bhumne—In the sky; Param—The supreme; Sarvavyapak—All-pervading;\nPurusha—The supreme bei