      "textEn": "He had pronounced, but he was saved from all the consequences of sin. The chanting of the holy name is so\nmangalprad (beneficial) that it can free everyone from the fruits of sinful deeds. But from this, it should not be concluded that a person, to remedy the consequences of sin, can continue to commit sin by performing Hare Krishna Kirtan. Instead, to be free from all sins,\none should be careful, and through the chanting of the Hare Krishna mantra, sins will be removed, this\none should never even think, because that is another offense. If, by chance, a devotee commits any\nsinful act, then God will forgive him, but a human should not deliberately commit sinful acts. Hearing, remembering, and increasing the valor, Hari (Lord Vishnu) is always with us.\nAs by the good deeds of a worthy devotee, by purity of heart, and by vows etc. 32. Meaning of the word\n\nShrunvatam—those who listen; Gruntatam—those who sing and do kirtan; Viryani—amazing deeds; Uddamani—remover of sins; KaraNa—capable; HareHa—of the complete Supreme Being; Muhuh—always; Yatha—as; Su-jataaya—easily in front; Laya—brought; Bhaktya—through devotion; Shuddhayet—can be purified; Na—not; Atma—heart and soul; Vrat-\nAdibhimah—by performing rituals..\n\nThe person who constantly listens to and sings the name of God, and listens to and sings the works of God,\ncan very easily attain the state of pure devotion,\nwhich is the one that purifies the dirt of his heart. Only by observing vows and performing Vedic\nrituals, such purification cannot be attained. Meaning: Man can easily practice chanting and listening to the name of God, and\nin this way, one can become ecstatic in spiritual life. The statement of Padma Purana is—\n\nThose who are sinners, even the smallest sin, are removed.\nThey are the ones who are free from restlessness and also the ones who are the meaning-makers. If a person performs the Hare Krishna Mahamantra's Kirtan even with a crime, then he is unyielding"
